                        "sense_id": "fb9400d0-0fe2-3e6b-9083-cba86d749e90",
                        "entry_id": "b8a82f40-d7b2-3326-ab8f-008b5652283e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A golf ball made from reclaimed materials."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f36dbd37-7e25-4300-826a-07e232e5caed",
                                "sense_id": "fb9400d0-0fe2-3e6b-9083-cba86d749e90",
                                "text": "While it is, unfortunately, true that a certain proportion of new balls crack—and a larger percentage of remades, doubtless incidental to the shell of the latter being made somewhat thinner in the remoulding process, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cae28f78-db2f-47e1-b956-be73ae990f0e",
                                "sense_id": "fb9400d0-0fe2-3e6b-9083-cba86d749e90",
                                "text": "George Fernie's nephew, Willie, testified that at least two dozen balls were made in 1893 and sold to players as 'remades' at 8d each."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
